Z||000000||Monkeyman||10-24-2001||06:07 AM||||I'm planning on relocating my HVAC controls to the place where the overhead lights are now.  Is there any reason why I couldn't lengthen the wires?  Can I use crimp on connectors (not very good with solder) or do I need to solder?  If so, for what reason?  Any other issues I should be aware of?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PontiacAPE.jpg">    <BR>Monkeyman||||reg||5
Z||000001||88CoupeV6||10-24-2001||11:09 AM||||The temp part is cable controlled. That would be the only real hard part.||||reg||4
Z||000002||theogre||10-24-2001||07:39 PM||||Electrically there's nothing to stop you moving them. Just the temperature door cable. That cable is usually picky about bend radius as well as twisting. To tight a bend and it may not work well or at all.<P>The wires can be crimped. I prefer non insulated crimps and heat shrink tubing myself. You can use standard insulated crimps as well. The same wire I mentioned for your mirror article would work well for this too. Use the correct crimping tool for your crimps and make sure they are tight.<P>Make sure the wire for the blower speed matches the gauge of the OE wire. A little heavier wouldn't be a bad idea. Those wire do carry some current.<P>The actuator wires and night light don't matter much as those are low current.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||10-24-2001||09:26 PM||||88CoupeV6--Thanx, but I would have to find a longer one anyway.<P>Mr. Ogre--I hadn't thought about kinking the temp cable.  Hopefully, I can mount this with enough space behind it so I can avoid this.  If not, I may still have to relocate the temp control.  (A PITA, but I think I could do it tastefully.)  I hadn't thought about using the wiring you described for my alternate mirror switch.  Good idea.  This would keep me from wiring it wrong.  There are alot of wires that run to the HVAC controls.  I wonder how many wires I can get in a trailer wiring kit?  4?  6?  More?<P>Do I need to upgrade all of the wiring that goes to the fan switch or just one of them?  I suppose it would be a good idea to upgrade all of them just to be safe, right?||||reg||1
