Z||000009||Monkeyman||10-25-2001||06:22 PM||||I know what you're saying, but I'd still end up with an entire control panel instead of just a small slider control.  The only advantage to using an A/C delete HVAC panel would be that it would already be calibrated for the control cable.  I'm assuming that the selections from Vintage Air are generic enough to allow me to use the stock cable.  Actually, I'm still hoping that I can make another cable work with the my stock HVAC panel.  That would solve all the problems.<P>UPDATE:::I bought a couple of truck/trailer wiring kits from Autozone.  Each has 4 wires.  I was thinking that there were only 8 wires on the back of the HVAC controls.  Umm...not.  There are 13.  I'll have to buy another kit tomorrow and then just add an extra wire by itself.  I also bought some 12ga wire for the fan switch wiring.  I'll use some non insulated crimp on connectors as theogre said.  I'll have to work on this tomorrow in case I need the defrost in the morning.||||reg||1
